# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-only
# id: parser.osc7-windows-drive-cwd
# geometry: 80 24
# expect-cwd: = /C:/Users/test
# expect-line: 0 =
#
# An OSC 7 working-directory report carrying a Windows drive-letter path, as
# emitted by the PowerShell shell integration. The path is DATA: the core
# percent-decodes it, validates the URL host, stores the string, and never
# touches a filesystem with it — so this expectation holds identically on
# Linux, macOS, and Windows, and its success says nothing about Windows
# process behavior.
#
# Escapes: \e ESC, \r CR, \n LF, \t HT, \\ backslash, \xNN one byte.
# Every other character is emitted literally. Lines add no implicit newline.

# Synthetic placeholder path from the validator's allowlist; BEL terminates.
\e]7;file://localhost/C:/Users/test\x07
